{
  "title": "China stops buying liquefied natural gas from US",
  "publication_date": "2023-11-16T00:00:00Z",
  "summary": "China has reportedly halted purchases of liquefied natural gas (LNG) from the United States, marking a significant shift in energy trade relations between the world's two largest economies.",
  "content": "China has ceased purchasing liquefied natural gas from the United States, according to recent reports. This development represents a notable change in the energy trade dynamics between the two major global economies.\n\nThe move comes amid ongoing trade tensions and China's efforts to diversify its energy supply sources. The decision could have significant implications for the US LNG export industry, which has seen substantial growth in recent years.\n\nThis shift in purchasing patterns may also impact global energy markets and prices, as China is one of the world's largest LNG importers.",
